os-dev-report
{
  "issue": 19953,
  "round": 2,
  "status": "done",
  "branch": "claude/issue-19953-rls-check-default-text",
  "pr": "https://github.com/objectstack-ai/objectstack/pull/19962",
  "head_sha": "22c9473c86d64d1e29b47548e2264affecd8a792",
  "commits_this_round": [
    "e2d9c7492e docs(spec, lint): scope the RLS check texts to the writes it runs on; limit OR-combine to reads",
    "22c9473c86 docs(spec): regenerate the security reference pages for the scoped check and priority texts (check:generated --fix output)"
  ],
  "session": "session_01Sfe5YjBLwB9J3y8fvm2xq1 — subagent of the domain:spec seat 5 PM",
  "premise_still_valid": true,
  "summary": "This round answers the blocking item ①.4 of contract review 5813145732, which I read in full. Every sentence in the PR diff that says or implies which writes are checked now names the measured scope: the new row of a single-record insert and of a by-id update. It also says that an array insert and a multi: true update are not post-image checked. The carriers #19964 and #19950 are cited in the TSDoc and the changeset only, because runtime and author-facing strings carry no tracker number. Composition ①.5a: the priority tombstone describe had its \"OR-combine (most permissive wins)\" reason cut, and the security.mdx:144 OR sentence is now limited to reads. The runtime is unchanged. The two generated reference pages were regenerated by check:generated --fix and not hand-edited.",
  "review_record": "5813145732 (VERDICT: FAIL at f139546003, blocking ①.4, non-blocking ①.5a/b/c). This round addresses ①.4 and ①.5a. ①.5b and ①.5c were not asked for and are unchanged.",
  "sentences_before_after": [
    {
      "where": "packages/spec/src/security/rls.zod.ts check describe (renders as references/security/rls.mdx:175 and permission.mdx:171)",
      "before": "Validation condition for INSERT/UPDATE, matched against the new row (enforced at application level).",
      "after": "Validation condition matched against the new row of a single-record INSERT or a by-id UPDATE (enforced at application level); an array insert and a `multi: true` update are not post-image checked.",
      "basis": "B1/B4 refuse a single-record insert of archived and store the array insert; A4/B4 store the multi-row update. The reviewer measured the same on both drivers."
    },
    {
      "where": "rls.zod.ts check TSDoc heading (was :397-400)",
      "before": "CHECK clause - Validation for INSERT/UPDATE operations. / Similar to USING but applies to new/modified rows. / Prevents users from creating/updating rows they wouldn't be able to see.",
      "after": "CHECK clause - Validation of the new row of a single-record INSERT or a by-id UPDATE. An array insert and a `multi: true` update are not post-image checked (#19964, #19950).",
      "basis": "Same cells. The \"Prevents users from creating/updating rows they wouldn't be able to see\" sentence was cut because it is measured false: C3 admits a single-record insert of closed, and that caller cannot read closed rows."
    },
    {
      "where": "rls.zod.ts check TSDoc, first Default Behavior bullet",
      "before": "its `using` is not part of the write check.",
      "after": "its `using` is not part of the check."
    },
    {
      "where": "rls.zod.ts priority retiredKey refusal (was :480; renders as rls.mdx:178 and permission.mdx:174)",
      "before": "It never had an effect and could not: applicable policies OR-combine (most permissive wins), so there is no conflict to order. Delete the key — policy outcomes are unchanged.",
      "after": "It never had an effect. Delete the key — policy outcomes are unchanged.",
      "basis": "A cut. The reason was false for the mixed write check (reviewer: pending 403; my C3/H1). The only test pin on this string is removed in @objectstack/spec 17.0.0, which still holds."
    },
    {
      "where": "rls.zod.ts file overview :81 (renders as references/security/rls.mdx:81, the same page as the check row) — bounded extension, same class",
      "before": "- Multiple policies OR-combine for union (any-match-allows) semantics",
      "after": "- Multiple policies OR-combine on reads (any match allows); for writes see `check`"
    },
    {
      "where": "rls.zod.ts file overview :95 (renders as rls.mdx:95) — bounded extension, same class",
      "before": "3. **Policy Precedence**: More permissive policy wins (OR logic) / 4. **Context Variables**: ...",
      "after": "The item is cut, and Context Variables is renumbered to 3."
    },
    {
      "where": "content/docs/permissions/rls.mdx:63 (property table)",
      "before": "Predicate the new row must satisfy **after an insert or update**. Omit it and `using` stands in, unless ...",
      "after": "Predicate the new row must satisfy **after a single-record insert or a by-id update**; an array insert and a `multi: true` update are not checked. Omit it and `using` stands in, unless ..."
    },
    {
      "where": "content/docs/permissions/rls.mdx:185-186 (How policies compose) — bounded extension, same page",
      "before": "— a row is admitted if it matches *any* applicable policy.",
      "after": "— on a read, a row is admitted if it matches *any* applicable policy (for writes, see item 4 of the fail-closed contract below)."
    },
    {
      "where": "content/docs/permissions/rls.mdx:205/208 (fail-closed item 4)",
      "before": "`using` stands in as the write check. ... a USING-only sibling's `using` is not part of the write check.",
      "after": "`using` stands in as the `check`. ... a USING-only sibling's `using` is not part of the check."
    },
    {
      "where": "content/docs/protocol/objectql/security.mdx:144 (named in ①.5a)",
      "before": "and/or a `check` clause (for INSERT/UPDATE) ... Multiple policies for one object are combined with OR (most-permissive wins).",
      "after": "and/or a `check` clause (for the new row of a single-record INSERT or a by-id UPDATE; an array insert and a `multi: true` update are not checked) ... On reads, multiple policies for one object are combined with OR; for the write `check`, see `RowLevelSecurityPolicySchema.check`."
    },
    {
      "where": "packages/lint/src/validate-rls-predicate-enforceability.ts header item 4",
      "before": "per insert / update and per caller: ... So an unlowerable `check` always reaches this path, and an unlowerable `using` on an `insert` / `update` / `all` policy reaches it whenever ...",
      "after": "per single-record insert / by-id update and per caller (an array insert and a `multi: true` update never reach it): ... So an unlowerable `check` on an `insert` / `update` / `all` policy reaches this path, and so does an unlowerable `using` on one whenever ...",
      "basis": "\"always\" was also false for select and delete policies (B3/B5 are never evaluated)."
    },
    {
      "where": "lint USING_INSERT_CONSEQUENCE (shipped in all three using findings)",
      "before": "the same `using` is also the INSERT check whenever ...",
      "after": "the same `using` is also the single-record INSERT check whenever ..."
    },
    {
      "where": "lint comments (not shipped strings)",
      "before": "reaches the insert too / beside a USING-only sibling, every write was refused",
      "after": "reaches the single-record insert too / beside a USING-only sibling, every single-record insert was refused",
      "basis": "D4 measured inserts only."
    },
    {
      "where": ".changeset/19953-rls-check-default-composition-text.md",
      "before": "no scope sentence; the lint bullet said \"that `using` is also the insert check\"",
      "after": "Added: \"The check runs on the new row of a single-record insert and of a by-id update. An array insert and a `multi: true` update are not post-image checked; those are tracked in #19964 and #19950, and the texts now say so instead of implying every insert and update is checked.\" The spec bullet now names the priority-refusal cut and the reads-only OR-combine. The lint bullet now says \"the single-record insert check\"."
    }
  ],
  "property_1_grep": {
    "command": "git diff 3b5607019f..HEAD -U0 | grep -E \"^\\+[^+]\" | grep -n -i -E \"insert|update|write|new row|post-image|INSERT/UPDATE|checked\" — 118 added lines in the whole PR diff, TSDoc and comments included. Each hit was read. Every one that states or implies which writes are checked now carries the single-record insert / by-id update scope, or makes no claim about coverage (applicability, composition, pointers).",
    "control": "Lit control on the old unscoped spellings. The pattern ORs 12 phrases: after an insert or update**; Validation condition for INSERT/UPDATE, matched; as the write check; not part of the write check; per insert / update and per caller; always reaches this path; also the INSERT check; every write was refused; most permissive wins), so there is no conflict; combined with OR (most-permissive wins); More permissive policy wins; union (any-match-allows). It was run with git grep -c over the 7 files the PR touches. At the round-1 head f139546003 it matched 18 lines. At 22c9473c86 it matches 0. Positive control inside the same grep: the already-qualified lint strings \"every single-record insert and by-id update\" still hit.",
    "remaining_unscoped_context": "Pre-existing and outside the diff: the `using` describe \"Filter condition for SELECT/UPDATE/DELETE ... Optional for INSERT-only policies\" (review ①.5c, not asked for). The overview best-practice \"Define INSERT/UPDATE CHECK Policies\" is guidance, not a coverage claim."
  },
  "property_2_composition": {
    "named_and_changed": [
      "priority tombstone describe (rls.zod.ts:480, and both reference rows): reason cut",
      "content/docs/protocol/objectql/security.mdx:144: OR limited to reads, with a pointer to check"
    ],
    "extended_same_class": [
      "rls.zod.ts overview :81 and :95, which render onto the same references/security/rls.mdx page as the new check row",
      "content/docs/permissions/rls.mdx:185, the same page as the rewritten check row"
    ],
    "not_touched_as_ordered": "packages/spec/src/migrations/registry.ts:159-160 is a landed migration entry, still saying \"applicable policies OR-combine (most permissive wins)\". The texts generated from the landed entries carry the same sentence and were not touched: docs/protocol-upgrade-guide.md:36 and :163, packages/spec/spec-changes.json:79 and :971, and the conversions/registry.ts:1908-1923 entry.",
    "residue_listed_not_edited": [
      "rls.zod.ts:463-466 priority TSDoc: \"Applicable policies OR-combine (any match allows access ... most-permissive-wins)\". This is a code comment, not rendered (0 hits in the reference page). It is the removal rationale, and its conclusion (no order to resolve) still holds.",
      "content/docs/permissions/authorization.mdx:108: \"Multiple row policies for the same object/operation OR-combine\". Same class on another page, not named in the order. Carrier: none.",
      "content/docs/releases/v17/17-0.mdx:644 is release-owned. ADR-0066:93, ADR-0092:369 and ADR-0095:79-81 are governed. The plugin-security comments (rls-compiler.ts:424 and :600, default-permission-sets.ts) are in the runtime lane.",
      "content/docs/permissions/sharing-rules.mdx:81 is about `using` widening, which OR-combines. It is true and was left alone."
    ]
  },
  "prose_delta": {
    "round_2_lines": "f139546003..22c9473c86 across 7 files: +42 / -41, net +1 line. Hand-written files only (excluding the two generated pages): +36 / -34, net +2. Generated pages: +6 / -7, net -1.",
    "round_2_words_supplement": "Line counts hide single-line table rows and describes, so words are given too (git diff --word-diff=porcelain). Hand-written +258 / -105, net +153, of which the changeset paragraph and bullets are the largest share. Generated pages +52 / -52, net 0.",
    "whole_pr": "3b5607019f..22c9473c86: +128 / -41 over 7 files."
  },
  "gates": {
    "spec_test": "pnpm --filter @objectstack/spec test: 529 files, 15602 passed, 1 todo. VERDICT command-exit 0.",
    "lint_test": "pnpm --filter @objectstack/lint test: 108 files, 4127 passed. VERDICT command-exit 0. The rule's own pins on ZERO rows, RLS_DENY_FILTER, PermissionDeniedError and blanket refusal hold.",
    "typecheck": "The typecheck scripts of @objectstack/spec and @objectstack/lint (Scope: 2 of 82): VERDICT command-exit 0. The test layers of both packages compile.",
    "check_generated": "The --fix run proved 1 of 15 artifacts stale (check:docs), regenerated only content/docs/references/**, and re-checked what it wrote. At 22c9473c86 the check:generated gate run printed: All 15 generated artifacts are up to date.",
    "dispatch_gates": "node scripts/pm/dispatch-gates.mjs --commands --repo objectstack-ai/objectstack at 22c9473c86 derived 101 commands from 7 paths. That is round 1's set minus 6 ADR/governed families, a subset. --ran: 101 derived, 100 run, 0 UNRUN, 1 NOT-MEASURED.",
    "not_measured": "NOT MEASURED: pnpm check:dual-build-cjs-loads, reason PREREQUISITE NOT MET (33 packages without dist in this worktree; no full build was run). CI Lint & Repo Gates runs it, and that check is success at this head.",
    "citation_gate": "node scripts/check-issue-citations.mjs --base origin/main (live): 2 added citations judged, 2 resolve (#19964, #19950 are open issues). Exit 0.",
    "governed": "node scripts/pm/check-governed-merges.mjs --pr 19962 after the push: \"governed-surface predicate: 0 of 7 path(s) hit the register (6 surfaces, repo-agnostic).\" and \"✅  NOT governed — ordinary queue landing applies to a PR with exactly this file list.\" Size 169 changed lines.",
    "eslint_narrowed": "npx eslint --no-inline-config --format json on the 2 touched TS files: 2 files, 0 errors, 0 warnings. eslint.config.mjs enables no type-aware linting, so the diff cannot move a verdict on an untouched file."
  },
  "ci": "Read at 22c9473c86, 12:07Z: 35 check-runs, 33 success, 2 skipped (Console Pin Gate, Packed-tarball smoke (opt-in)), 0 in progress, 0 failed. All seven required contexts are success: Lint & Repo Gates, TypeScript Type Check, Test Core (rollup and 1-6/6), Dogfood Regression Gate (rollup and 1-3/3), Build Core, Temporal Conformance (live PG + MySQL), Governed Surface Queue Guard.",
  "mcp_calls": "0",
  "api_writes": "This round: 1, this os-dev-report comment through scripts/pm/post-stamped.mjs from a detached origin/main worktree. dispatch.mjs --route read transport dispatch, and the relay executed it as POST /repos/objectstack-ai/objectstack/issues/19953/comments. Plus git pushes of e2d9c7492e and 22c9473c86 (not REST). No PR body, label, ready or merge writes.",
  "open_questions": [],
  "out_of_scope_findings": [
    "carrier: 承接者:无 · noted, not filed — content/docs/permissions/authorization.mdx:108 still says \"Multiple row policies for the same object/operation OR-combine\" without the write-check exception (same class as review ①.5a, not named in the order).",
    "carrier: 承接者:无 · noted, not filed — review ①.5b is unchanged: security-plugin.ts:837-838 and rls-check-defaults-to-using.test.ts:5-6 quote the old describe, and packages/spec/liveness/permission.json:204 quotes check ?? policy.using. Review ①.5c is also unchanged: the `using` describe and TSDoc do not say the `using` is the insert check when no check is declared.",
    "Already filed and cited as carriers: #19964 (array insert not post-image checked), #19950 (multi-row update), #19965 (check on select or delete policies)."
  ],
  "deviations": [
    "Beyond the two ①.5a texts named in the order, I qualified three more of the same class that sit on pages this PR already rewrites: rls.zod.ts overview :81 and :95, which render onto references/security/rls.mdx, and permissions/rls.mdx:185. I also scoped the \"(for INSERT/UPDATE)\" clause on the security.mdx:144 line I was editing, per property 1. The reason: leaving them would put a contradiction on the same generated page as the new check row.",
    "The PR body still describes the ADR note and the Tier H landing, and I did not edit it (no PR body writes). The seat rewrites it."
  ],
  "cleanup": "Worktree ../objectstack-issue-19953-r2 was clean (git status empty) and its HEAD equals the origin branch at 22c9473c86. Its node_modules is removed and the worktree is removed with git worktree remove, no --force, after this comment posts. The posting worktree ../objectstack-19953-post2 (detached at origin/main) is removed the same way. No dev server, watcher or monitor was left. The gate runner was waited on by its own recorded PID, and nothing was killed."
}
